FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE

TITLE: Bemba and Lozi Proposed as Zambia’s Official National Languages

LUSAKA, Zambia – A landmark bill titled “The National Languages (Official Status) Bill, 2025” has been officially submitted to the National Assembly. Authored by Major Dr. Kabanga Allan, the bill seeks to induct Bemba and Lozi as co-official languages of Zambia, supported by 2020 Census data showing 53% fluency in Bemba and significant use of Lozi.

The bill outlines a roadmap for legal, educational, and administrative integration by 2029 and is backed by traditional leadership and academic stakeholders. This marks a bold step toward linguistic decolonization and civic inclusion.

